# livediagram MCP server (spec/62). No secrets live here: the MCP forwards the
# caller's Bearer lvd_ token to the api worker over a service binding, and the
# OAuth consent + token mint authenticate via Clerk in apps/live + apps/api.
#
# Configure via wrangler, not env vars:
#   - the API service binding (apps/api) — see wrangler.toml
#   - the OAUTH_KV namespace: `wrangler kv namespace create OAUTH_KV`, then put
#     the id in wrangler.toml
#
# Optional [vars] (wrangler.toml or `wrangler secret put`):
#   - CONSENT_BASE_URL: origin of the live app that serves the OAuth consent
#     page (`/oauth/consent`). Defaults to https://livediagram.app, so a
#     self-host serving the editor on its own domain must point this at that
#     origin or OAuth callers land on the hosted consent screen instead.
# CONSENT_BASE_URL=https://livediagram.app
#   - INTERNAL_EVENTS_KEY: shared secret (a worker secret) that marks this
#     worker's telemetry posts as internal, so the api doesn't put them in
#     the anonymous per-IP rate-limit bucket (spec/22). A service binding
#     sends no CF-Connecting-IP, so without this every MCP tool call in the
#     world contends for one 120/min key. Must MATCH the api worker's
#     INTERNAL_EVENTS_KEY; unset on either side just restores the old
#     shared-bucket behaviour, so it is safe to skip on a self-host.
# INTERNAL_EVENTS_KEY=<random string>
#
# The MCP is gated on auth being enabled end-to-end: with Clerk unset, the
# api's /api/oauth/exchange rejects every caller and the consent page has no
# signed-in user, so no token can be minted (spec/62 §3.7). A no-auth
# self-host simply doesn't deploy this worker.
